       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Purpose.** Draw the equilibrium the way the notes do: tightness $\\theta$ on the vertical axis of both panels, vacancy supply and wage setting crossing at $(w^{*}, \\theta^{*})$ on the left, and $\\theta^{*}$ carried across to the Beveridge curve on the right. Dashed curves stay at the practice numbers, so each shift in the notes' table can be seen against where it started.\n- **Model.** A view of [Search and Matching Equilibrium Model](note:search-and-matching-equilibrium-model) ($\\alpha = 1/2$).\n- **Elements.** Panel `wages`: curves `vs_curve`, `ws_curve`, `vs_base`, `ws_base`; points `eq`, `eq_base`. Panel `beveridge`: curves `bc_curve`, `bc_base`; line `th_line`; points `eq_u`, `eq_u_base`. Readouts `theta_out`, `w_out`, `f_out`, `u_out`."
      }
     ],
